CORE dfcc-only
weak.c
--dfcc main --enforce-contract f _ --pointer-check
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[precondition_instance\.1\] .*static array parameter x must provide access to its declared minimum: FAILURE$
^\[f\.assertion\.1\] .*implementation is reachable: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^\[main\.precondition_instance\.
^\s*ASSUME .*r_ok\(f::
--
A function's own contract that is weaker than its [static N] minimum cannot be
enforced. The contract-checking wrapper does not assume the generated
static-array requires clause, so the implementation stays reachable, and the
minimum fails at the call to the wrapped implementation, as it does for a
separately named contract.
